#!/bin/sh
# A short map from kind of challenge to the tools already installed in this box.
cat <<'HELP'

  Which tool for which challenge
  ------------------------------
  Any file      file X            what is it, really?
                strings X         readable text inside
                xxd X | less      the raw bytes
  Encodings     base64 -d         decode base64
                tr 'A-Za-z' 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m'    ROT13
                python3           for anything else (XOR, Caesar loops, ...)
  Images        exiftool X        hidden metadata
                zbarimg X         read a QR code
                pngcheck -v X     check a PNG's structure
                binwalk X         files hidden inside files
                zsteg X           common hiding tricks in PNG
                steghide extract -sf X
                convert X -auto-level out.png   (then scp it to your laptop)
  Documents     pdfinfo X, exiftool X
  Archives      tar -xzf X, unzip X, 7z x X
  Network       tshark -r X       read a capture
                tshark -r X -Y http -T fields -e http.request.uri
                curl URL          fetch a web page, see headers with -i
  Audio         sox X -n spectrogram -o out.png   (then scp it to your laptop)
                multimon-ng       decoders for tones and Morse
  Programs      ./X               run it (chmod +x X first)
                ltrace ./X        library calls, often the password check
                strace ./X        system calls
                gdb ./X           step through it
                objdump -d X      read the machine code

  Every tool has a manual:  man <tool>   (q to quit)
  Stuck? Each challenge has hints on the game site, and the tutorials explain the basics.
  Or ask the AI helper:  ai "what is this?" < FILE    (ai --help for more)

HELP
